// Deck: gs-01-why-reqlan — authored JSONC; sync emits runtime decks/gs-01-why-reqlan.json for the player.
{
  "id": "gs-01-why-reqlan",
  "title": "Why requirements as code",
  "series": "get-started",
  "transition": "fade",
  "slides": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "brand-dark",
      "content": {
        "kicker": "Get started · 01",
        "heading": "Why requirements as code",
        "asset": "logo"
      },
      "notes": "If you work with language models on real projects, you already write requirements — you just write them into the chat window, over and over."
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "brand-panel",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Context drift is familiar",
        "body": "You paste the same intent into chat again and again."
      },
      "notes": "Every new thread starts from scratch unless you rebuild context by hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "contrast",
      "transition": "none",
      "background": "brand-contrast",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Chat dump vs named ideas",
        "body": "Same intent. Two shapes — only one stays findable.",
        "code_label": "chat paste",
        "code": "Users must log in. Empty passwords fail.\nSessions time out. Failed attempts get logged.\nAlso remember rate limits somehow…",
        "code_lang": "txt",
        "code_b_label": "named ideas",
        "code_b": "login must reject empty passwords\nsession expires after inactivity\naudit_log records failed attempts",
        "code_b_lang": "rq"
      },
      "notes": "reqlan turns that intent into a graph of named ideas — requirements as code."
    },
    {
      "id": "loop",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "brand-panel",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Name, prose, neighbours",
        "body": "Editor language support · activity bar neighbourhood · optional graph map.",
        "asset": "montage-ide"
      },
      "notes": "Day one is name the idea, write the prose, point at related work."
    },
    {
      "id": "misconception",
      "transition": "none",
      "background": "brand-contrast",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Not another notes app",
        "body": "Notes store paragraphs. reqlan stores handles you can link and search."
      },
      "notes": "You do not need a schema on day one — you need names your tools can reuse."
    },
    {
      "id": "install",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "brand-panel",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Install the extension",
        "body": "Extensions view → search “reqlan” → Install. Any folder works — an empty one is fine."
      },
      "notes": "The reqlan icon joins the activity bar after install. The welcome webview appears on first launch."
    },
    {
      "id": "onboarding",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "brand-panel",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Welcome, not base yet",
        "body": "Keep docs and marketplace links from the onboarding page."
      },
      "notes": "Creating a base with .reqlan comes after you have written a few ideas."
    },
    {
      "id": "end",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "brand-dark",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Semantic requirements as code, built for LLM workflows",
        "asset": "logo",
        "fragments": [
          "Next: Your first idea"
        ]
      },
      "notes": "Next: write your first idea in under a minute."
    }
  ]
}
